<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45350" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stercus</span></b> , ŏris, n.
		Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκώρ</span>; <i>gen.</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκατός</span>, dung; Sanscr. cakrt =
			sakart. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>dung</i>, <i>excrements</i>, <i>ordure</i> (syn.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fimus, merda),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 38</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 2, 15</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">37</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Div. 1, 27, 57</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor.
				Epod. 12, 11 al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				344</span></i> Müll.; cf. <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 6, § 32</span></i> ib., and
			Fest. s. v. Quando stercus, pp. 258 and 259 ib.; <i><span class="en">Juv. 14,
			64</span></i>.—Prov.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurum in stercore quaerere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Inst. Div. Lit. 1, p. 510</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> As a
			term of abuse: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nolo stercus curiae dici Glauciam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 3, 41, 164</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ferri,</span>”
				i. e. <i>dross</i>, <i>slag</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 188</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
